<title>HUNGARY: OTP group '96 after-tax profit 10.39 bln.</title>
<headline>OTP group '96 after-tax profit 10.39 bln.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-02-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year 1996, ending December 31.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of forints unless stated)</p>
<p>					   Jan-Dec 1996     Jan-Dec 1995</p>
<p>    Group operating profit	  18,456.1    vs    11,754.8</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit	    13,882.6    vs     9,198.5</p>
<p>    Group after-tax profit	  10,386.0    vs     7,180.9</p>
<p>    Group net interest income     59,123.1   vs     57,377.2</p>
<p>    Interest receieved	     203,388.4   vs    185,177.8</p>
<p>    Interest paid		    144,265.3   vs    127,800.6</p>
<p>    Dividend received		    324.4   vs	  436.8</p>
<p>Other revenue from</p>
<p>     banking activity		 33,996.9   vs     26,831.9</p>
<p>    Other revenue			7,871.6   vs     32,385.3</p>
<p>    Costs of banking activity     41,409.9   vs     35,500.3</p>
<p>Revenue from non-banking</p>
<p>	activity			  42,264.5   vs     15,346.3</p>
<p>Expenditures on non-banking</p>
<p>	activity			  45,951.2   vs     18,219.6</p>
<p>    Net extraordinary income	   886.8 loss vs 317.0 profit</p>
<p>    Taxation			     3,368.1   vs	2,010.0</p>
<p>NOTE - OTP Bank is Hungary's largest commercial bank. The figures are consolidated and they were prepared in accordance with Hungarian Accounting Standards. The 1996 figures are not audited.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom +36 1 327-4040</p>
</text>
